<Shell title="Own the system your site depends on." direction="C / Ownership first" theme="dark">
  <section class="frame hero-ownership"><div><span class="micro">Open-source site control / In development</span><h1>Own the system<br />your site<br /><span>depends on.</span></h1><p>Origin89 is building an open stack for remote and off-grid sites. Connect equipment from different makers, run control locally, and keep the ability to understand and extend your system.</p><div class="actions"><a class="action" href="/next/open/">Explore the open stack <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-action" href="/next/equipment/">Find your equipment ↗</a></div></div><figure class="ownership-art"><img src={art.board} alt="CAD render exposing the Controller circuit board" width="1200" height="1824" fetchpriority="high" /><span class="ownership-side" aria-hidden="true">ORIGIN89 / CONTROLLER</span><figcaption class="micro">Existing CAD model · Concept hardware</figcaption></figure></section>
  <div class="frame ownership-proof"><div><strong>Hardware</strong><span>Designs you can inspect</span></div><div><strong>Firmware</strong><span>Control you can understand</span></div><div><strong>Apps</strong><span>Views you can adapt</span></div><div><strong>Interfaces</strong><span>Connections you can extend</span></div></div>
  <section class="frame manifesto"><span class="micro">What ownership should mean</span><h2>The pump may outlast your phone.<br /><span>Your site needs a system<br />you can keep working on.</span></h2><p>Openness becomes useful when it gives an owner or installer a way to inspect behaviour, adapt a connection and maintain a setup over time. That is the standard we want Origin89 to meet.</p><a class="text-action" href="/next/open/" style="margin-top:25px">See the source and release status ↗</a></section>
  <div class="white-section"><section class="frame section-pad two-column"><div><span class="micro">Start with the physical site</span><h2>Built for the equipment<br />you’ve chosen.</h2></div><div><p style="font-size:20px">Solar controllers, battery systems, generator interfaces, pumps and field sensors. Browse the research behind our integration work, then tell us what matters on your site.</p><div class="actions"><a class="action" href="/next/equipment/">Browse equipment <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-action" href="/next/sample-site/">See a sample site ↗</a></div></div></section><Products /></div><CTA />
